# tools/hunk_scroll_fling_witness.rish — the fling: momentum decay after the finger lifts (HUNK45).
#
# Season A (Hardware & Right-to-Repair) · waymark HUNK · marketplace / Photos-app surface · rung HUNK45.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-200615_hunk-scroll-fling-exploration.md.
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: the momentum layer of any touch scroll surface — after the finger lifts a flick keeps
# coasting, its velocity decaying under friction until it settles to rest (concept only, siloed).
#
# HUNK43 routed a raw event; HUNK44 quantized a pixel drag with a carried remainder. This rung is the gesture after the
# finger lifts: `pond/apps/preset_scroll_fling.rye` `Fling` is a signed pixels-per-tick velocity that strictly decreases
# in magnitude every tick and settles to rest, each tick's delta fed through HUNK44's `drag` so the cursor's clamps are
# inherited (a hard fling lands bottom-pinned, never past) and the sign never flips. The friction and velocity bounds
# let the tick count be asserted — a fling always settles within a small ceiling. The selftest flings a two-row viewport
# over a real five-book library and proves the monotone settle, the sign stability, the no-overshoot clamp, the
# immediate-done zero fling, and the friction/velocity refusals. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/hunk_scroll_fling_witness.rish

say "hunk-scroll-fling: Language EN — HUNK45 gives a lifted finger its momentum: a fling coasts, its velocity decaying under friction until it settles to rest, every tick clamped by the cursor beneath — no network, no key, no funds."
say "hunk-scroll-fling: Style Radiant — a flick is a velocity that remembers it is slowing down; friction is only honest when it always comes to rest, and this seam proves it always does."
say "hunk-scroll-fling: Lens TAME — a pure decay over a bounded velocity, positive invariants per fn, the decay taken in i64 so velocity*num never wraps; the friction and velocity caps make the tick count an assertion, not a hope."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "pond/apps/bin/preset_scroll_fling"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p pond/apps/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build pond/apps/preset_scroll_fling.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "hunk-scroll-fling: build failed — ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "hunk-scroll-fling: selftest exited non-zero — ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "hunk-scroll-fling: ${out}"

assert out contains "GREEN preset-scroll-fling" else "hunk-scroll-fling: selftest did not print the GREEN preset-scroll-fling line"

assert out contains "decays strictly to rest without flipping sign" else "hunk-scroll-fling: the monotone sign-stable decay was not proven"

assert out contains "its velocity never turning positive" else "hunk-scroll-fling: the upward-fling sign stability was not proven"

assert out contains "lands exactly on the bottom-pinned offset and a hard upward one on the top with no overshoot" else "hunk-scroll-fling: the no-overshoot clamp was not proven"

assert out contains "the gentlest allowed friction (7/8) at a large speed still settles within the ceiling" else "hunk-scroll-fling: the bounded-tick ceiling was not proven"

assert out contains "a zero-velocity fling is immediately done and never moves" else "hunk-scroll-fling: the immediate-done zero fling was not proven"

assert out contains "each refuse by name" else "hunk-scroll-fling: the friction/velocity refusals were not proven"

say "hunk-scroll-fling: GREEN — a lifted finger's fling coasts and always settles: the velocity decays strictly without flipping sign, a hard flick clamps at the ends with no overshoot, a zero fling never moves, and the friction and velocity bounds refuse by name. HUNK44 drag, HUNK43 input, and HUNK40 cursor GREEN beneath."
